// No solutions here: a problem without `s` shows "no written solution on the site for now" and the official paper is the reference.
// Maths between \( \) or \[ \]; the strings are String.raw, so the backslashes are written once. The host city of
// each edition is general knowledge, not read from the official site [VERIFY].
